{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788217708160,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eb3c6effeTntrFS9ccOqRTL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-93fa00d4ed1090aa","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 170"},"output":"title:\tErlang backend: empirical toolchain verification (follow-up to #163)\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t170\n--\nRound answer (module-routing-and-erlang-target grilling round, question erlang-target-consideration): maintainer chose to go beyond plans/erlang-target-research.md's desk-only research and actually verify the Erlang toolchain empirically (process/effect model, selective receive, pattern matching) against real erl/erlc output. Note: a prior run of #163's own research spike tried a toolchain presence check (which erl / erl -eval) and was denied by sandbox policy (see plans/opencode-rollout.md, incident 2026-09-01) -- that is an infrastructure-level restriction, not something a rebrief alone fixes. If this run hits the same denial, document precisely what was denied and stop rather than retrying through another channel; that is itself a valid, useful finding to report back. Maintainer also flagged: concurrency will need to be supported by toylang regardless of this backend question -- worth surfacing as its own open item once this lands.\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tErlang backend: empirical toolchain verification (follow-up to #163)\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t170\n--\nRound answer (module-routing-and-erlang-target grilling round, question erlang-target-consideration): maintainer chose to go beyond plans/erlang-target-research.md's desk-only research and actually verify the Erlang toolchain empirically (process/effect model, selective receive, pattern matching) against real erl/erlc output. Note: a prior run of #163's own research spike tried a toolchain presence check (which erl / erl -eval) and was denied by sandbox policy (see plans/opencode-rollout.md, incident 2026-09-01) -- that is an infrastructure-level restriction, not something a rebrief alone fixes. If this run hits the same denial, document precisely what was denied and stop rather than retrying through another channel; that is itself a valid, useful finding to report back. Maintainer also flagged: concurrency will need to be supported by toylang regardless of this backend question -- worth surfacing as its own open item once this lands.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 170","time":{"start":1788217708155,"end":1788217708158}},"id":"prt_05a14caee001in2FVVuSl5ekun","sessionID":"ses_fa5eb3c6effeTntrFS9ccOqRTL","messageID":"msg_05a14c46d001fb4f4Y07oVLCkX"}}
