{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788217717480,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eb3c6effeTntrFS9ccOqRTL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a78b68486fa93378","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 163"},"output":"title:\tConsider Erlang as an additional backend target, as a design stress test\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t163\n--\nCaptured from a maintainer compose note (docs/.annotations/notes.json), unscheduled backlog idea:\n\n\"we could consider erlang as a target language too to further stress test our design\"\n\nNo investigation done yet into what Erlang's semantics would demand of toylang's design (e.g. its own take on processes/effects, pattern matching, immutability) or how it'd compare to the seven backends that exist today (Lua, JS, Native/LLVM, jq, Go, Python, Rust).\n\nWritten by the drive-loop coordinator session.\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tConsider Erlang as an additional backend target, as a design stress test\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t163\n--\nCaptured from a maintainer compose note (docs/.annotations/notes.json), unscheduled backlog idea:\n\n\"we could consider erlang as a target language too to further stress test our design\"\n\nNo investigation done yet into what Erlang's semantics would demand of toylang's design (e.g. its own take on processes/effects, pattern matching, immutability) or how it'd compare to the seven backends that exist today (Lua, JS, Native/LLVM, jq, Go, Python, Rust).\n\nWritten by the drive-loop coordinator session.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 163","time":{"start":1788217717475,"end":