 variant declarations that don't start with a capital letter, per the curly-only-pattern ruling (gh:156 ruling)\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: match-type-wrapper-experiment\n  issue: gh:122\n  title: 'Experimentally build a Match<T> wrapper: `.` entering a `|` chain wraps as Match<T>, traits like `%` get generic impls over Match<T> per underlying T (applying only past a passing boolean guard), and an arm''s aliases become named fields on a result struct the match produces -- see what goes wrong before ratifying (gh:122 ruling)'\n  kind: build\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n- id: partial-application-system-design\n  issue: gh:119\n  title: 'Grill array-like vs struct-like partial application for the colon method-call operator (gh:119 ruling spinoff) -- maintainer: \"either five_plus(1) is correct (but still becomes curried) or five_plus [1, 2] is correct; also function will still always only have one parameter; a true curried function would be a function that returns another function; we may want to implement this, or perhaps consider instead thinking about formalizing at least the beginning of a partial application system which could either apply a partial array-like or a partial struct-like\"'\n  kind: decide\n  needs: []\n  status: todo\n\n\n\n- id: draft-core-model-migration","lineStart":155,"lineEnd":194,"totalLines":310,"truncated":true}},"title":"plans/board.yaml","time":{"start":1788217722364,"end":1788217722368}},"id":"prt_05a1504a3001tPKjXnAtljKVTL","sessionID":"ses_fa5eb3c6effeTntrFS9ccOqRTL","messageID":"msg_05a14f302001HfNc0GMPi9cnvK"}}
