{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788217726129,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eb3c6effeTntrFS9ccOqRTL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-92bd9d56d94eb5db","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git show --stat 9b9cec3 | head -30; echo \"=== rollout incident commit ===\"; git show --stat 9a6f42c | head -30"},"output":"commit 9b9cec3270705d41c1abbaf1f7e72d68edadc610\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 00:39:48 2026 +0200\n\n    Research Erlang as a target: stress test, not a backend\n    \n    Survey of Erlang's actor/message-passing model against toylang's cardinality and\n    effect layer, the matcher, and the seven existing backends. Erlang's one distinct\n    axis (concurrency, selective receive) is absent from the toylang language, so an\n    eighth emitter would never exercise it and duplicates existing witnesses on every\n    used axis; it fails the backends-as-falsifiers admission test. Worth keeping as a\n    documented probe of Q4 (out-of-order consumption) and Q35 (output as effect).\n    \n    Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode\n\n plans/erlang-target-research.md | 177 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 177 insertions(+)\n=== rollout incident commit ===\ncommit 9a6f42c7bd324ec7b9a21811190b73d497b7a274\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 00:37:42 2026 +0200\n\n    opencode-rollout.md: log the erlang-target-research toolchain-denial incident\n    \n    Captured by a live drive tick, not authored in this interactive\n    session -- committing per the Stop hook's uncommitted-work check.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n plans/opencode-rollout.md | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)\n","metadata":{"output":"commit 9b9cec3270705d41c1abbaf1f7e72d68edadc610\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 00:39:48 2026 +0200\n\n    Research Erlang as a target: stress test, not a backend\n    \n    Survey of Erlang's actor/message-passing model against toylang's cardinality and\n    effect layer, the matcher, and the seven existing backends. Erlang's one distinct\n    axis (concurrency, selective receive) is absent from the toylang language, so an\n    eighth emitter would never exercise it and duplicates existing witnesses on every\n    used axis; it fails the backends-as-falsifiers admission test. Worth keeping as a\n    documented probe of Q4 (out-of-order consumption) and Q35 (output as effect).\n    \n    Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode\n\n plans/erlang-target-research.md | 177 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 177 insertions(+)\n=== rollout incident commit ===\ncommit 9a6f42c7bd324ec7b9a21811190b73d497b7a274\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 00:37:42 2026 +0200\n\n    opencode-rollout.md: log the erlang-target-research toolchain-denial incident\n    \n    Captured by a live drive tick, not authored in this interactive\n    session -- committing per the Stop hook's uncommitted-work check.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n plans/opencode-rollout.md | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git show --stat 9b9cec3 | head -30; echo \"=== rollout incident commit ===\"; git show --stat 9a6f42c | head -30","time":{"start":1788217726126,"end":1788217726128}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"There's a commit 9b9cec3 \"Research Erlang as a target: stress test, not a backend\" that modified plans/erlang-target-research.md. But the file doesn't exist now. That's strange. Wait — maybe the commit was on a different branch, or the file was deleted. Let me check what commit 9b9cec3 did, and whether the file exists in the git history. Since git log --all found it, let me see the file content from that commit.\n\nAlso commit 9a6f42c \"opencode-rollout.md: log the erlang-target-research toolchain-denial incident\" — but my grep for \"2026-09-01\" or \"erl\" found nothing in opencode-rollout.md. That's odd. Maybe the grep didn't match because the content differs. Let me check these commits.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05a15128a001ADWKWWPZMi9vdm","sessionID":"ses_fa5eb3c6effeTntrFS9ccOqRTL","messageID":"msg_05a150620001012S3W3YlOjQ6F"}}
