{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788217736416,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eb3c6effeTntrFS9ccOqRTL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-98ed551e6e0e5f2e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git branch -a --contains 9a6f42c; echo \"=== current branch contains? ===\"; git merge-base --is-ancestor 9a6f42c HEAD && echo \"9a6f42c IS ancestor of HEAD\" || echo \"9a6f42c NOT ancestor\"; git merge-base --is-ancestor 9b9cec3 HEAD && echo \"9b9cec3 IS ancestor\" || echo \"9b9cec3 NOT ancestor\""},"output":"+ main\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -> origin/main\n  remotes/origin/main\n=== current branch contains? ===\n9a6f42c NOT ancestor\n9b9cec3 NOT ancestor\n","metadata":{"output":"+ main\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -> origin/main\n  remotes/origin/main\n=== current branch contains? ===\n9a6f42c NOT ancestor\n9b9cec3 NOT ancestor\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git branch -a --contains 9a6f42c; echo \"=== current branch contains? ===\"; git merge-base --is-ancestor 9a6f42c HEAD && echo \"9a6f42c IS ancestor of HEAD\" || echo \"9a6f42c NOT ancestor\"; git merge-base --is-ancestor 9b9cec3 HEAD && echo \"9b9cec3 IS ancestor\" || echo \"9b9cec3 NOT ancestor\"","time":{"start":1788217736413,"end":1788217736414}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I understand the full picture. The prior run (gh:163) attempted a toolchain presence check (`which erl escript erlc; erl -eval '...'`) and was denied by the sandbox permission system. The desk research was written to plans/erlang-target-research.md in commit 9b9cec3, but that commit is on the issue-163 branch, not on my issue-170 branch.\n\nThe task brief references the toolchain denial incident (2026-09-01) and says to read plans/erlang-target-research.md (existing desk research). But the file doesn't exist on my branch. Let me check whether the file is on the issue-163 branch and read its content so I understand the desk research, then I'll create it on my branch as needed.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. My branch issue-170 is the follow-up. The prior erlang research (9b9cec3) is on issue-163 branch. But the issue-170 issue says \"follow-up to #163\" and \"maintainer chose to go beyond plans/erlang-target-research.md's desk-only research and actually verify the Erlang toolchain empirically.\"\n\nSo the desk research file exists on the issue-163 branch. Since my task is the follow-up on issue-170, I need to read that desk research for context. Let me read it from the issue-163 branch.\n\nAlso, the incident referenced is in opencode-rollout.md (commit 9a6f42c). But that commit isn't on my branch either — my grep of opencode-rollout.md found nothing for \"erl\" or \"2026-09-01\". Let me check whether 9a6f42c is on my branch.\n\nActually, my earlier grep of the CURRENT opencode-rollout.md found no erlang content. Let me verify the current state of the file on my branch. The incident commit 9a6f42c — is it in my branch history? Let me check.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05a1539a90016Knncw2HkfsIIm","sessionID":"ses_fa5eb3c6effeTntrFS9ccOqRTL","messageID":"msg_05a1522a5001YS2bNz5ZkEwQ3p"}}
